            'Clothing is a basic human need that has evolved from protecting the body to reflecting personality, culture, and fashion trends. The apparel industry designs and manufactures clothing, closely linked with the textile industry (producing fibre, yarn, fabric) and the fashion industry (creating unique, branded clothing). Traditional craftsmanship, like embroidery, is now adapted into high-fashion wear, often involving community members in the design process. For example, nomadic communities\' traditional attire is being transformed into embroidered jackets and accessories for global markets.',
